.TH SDL_MAIN_NEEDED 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_MAIN_NEEDED \- Defined if the target platform _requires_ a special mainline through SDL.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_main.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_MAIN_NEEDED
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This won\(aqt be defined otherwise\[char46] If defined, SDL\(aqs headers will redefine
.BR main
to
.BR SDL_main \[char46]
.PP
This macro is defined by
.BR SDL_main\[char46]h ,
which is not automatically included by
.BR SDL\[char46]h \[char46]
.PP
Even if required, an app can define
.BR SDL_MAIN_HANDLED
and provide their own, if they know what they\(aqre doing\[char46]
.PP
This macro is used internally by SDL, and apps probably shouldn\(aqt rely on it\[char46]

